{
 "title": "Text processing: std.string",
 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Text has two forms in Greengold: **`str`** (immutable, a view: `\"hello\"`) and **`string`** (a UTF-8 sequence that can grow on the heap). `std.string` offers helpers that work with both."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "import std.string",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    text = \"  apple,pear,banana  \"",
    "    trimmed = string.str_trim(text)",
    "    print(trimmed)",
    "    print(string.str_contains(trimmed, \"pear\"))",
    "    print(string.str_starts_with(trimmed, \"apple\"))",
    "    parts = string.str_split(trimmed, ',')",
    "    print(parts.len)",
    "    for p in parts:",
    "        print(p)"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "apple,pear,banana",
    "true",
    "true",
    "3",
    "apple",
    "pear",
    "banana"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "To build a growable `string` use `string.from`, `append_str` and `append_byte`; to print it you take the read-only view with `as_str()`. Number conversions return `Optional`: `parse_i64`, `parse_f64`."
  },
  {
   "t": "code",
   "code": [
    "import std.string",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    msg = string.from(\"Greengold\")",
    "    msg.append_str(\" Language\")",
    "    msg.append_byte('!')",
    "    print(msg.as_str())",
    "    print(string.parse_i64(\"42\").value_or(0))",
    "    print(string.parse_i64(\"4x2\").value_or(-1))",
    "    print(string.to_upper(\"hello\").as_str())"
   ],
   "run": true,
   "output": [
    "Greengold Language!",
    "42",
    "-1",
    "HELLO"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "exercise",
   "id": "c10-l02-x1",
   "prompt": "Split the text `\"1,2,3,4\"` at the commas, convert each part with `parse_i64` and print their total.",
   "starter": [
    "import std.string",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    total: i64 = 0",
    "    print(total)"
   ],
   "solution": [
    "import std.string",
    "",
    "fn main():",
    "    total: i64 = 0",
    "    parts = string.str_split(\"1,2,3,4\", ',')",
    "    for p in parts:",
    "        total += string.parse_i64(p).value_or(0)",
    "    print(total)"
   ],
   "hint": "Split with `str_split`, add `parse_i64(p).value_or(0)` in a loop.",
   "expected": [
    "10"
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "quiz",
   "id": "c10-l02-q1",
   "q": "What does `string.parse_i64(\"abc\")` return?",
   "options": [
    "0",
    "`None` (an `Optional`)",
    "The program crashes"
   ],
   "answer": 1,
   "why": "Text that cannot be converted gives `None`; the failure is expressed as a value."
  }
 ]
}
